  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 342 AM CDT Wed Jul 22 2026\n\nWith Tropical Storm Bertha continuing to move slowly west along \nthe Gulf Coast today, we will see an uptick in\nnortherly/northeasterly breezes. This won't bring a relief from\nthe heat and humidity, however. The influence of ridging aloft,\nand deeper moisture especially in the zone along the Mississippi\nRiver valley, will result in peak heat index values of around 110\nto 115 degrees at most locations. There is a slight chance for\nshowers or thunderstorms in the region today, but heavy rain is\nexpected to stay south of our area.\n\nA cool front stalling in the region today will serve as a focus \nfor afternoon shower and thunderstorm development into the \nweekend. At least some limited heat stress is expected for Friday\nand Saturday, and then expanding influence from the ridge aloft is\nlikely to push us back into Elevated and Significant heat stress\nby early next week. /NF/",
